# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Rules are evaluated top to bottom, first match wins;
# specific redirects must sit above any catch-all SPA fallback (/* /index.html 200).
# O1 (2026-11-10): this rule only takes effect when the deploy attaches _redirects
# as deployment config (a form field on the deployment-create request, the way
# wrangler does it). Uploading it as an ordinary manifest asset makes Pages serve
# it as a static file and ignore the rules entirely — that is why this 301 did
# not fire on the live site until the deploy script was fixed (see the fixed
# deploy script handed to the coordinator with this work).
/manifest.webmanifest /manifest.json 301
